## Real example from this project

Query: `"money back for working from home"` — no exact keyword overlap with
the document title "Work From Home Reimbursement" beyond "working"/"home".

**TF-IDF result** (`search/keyword_search/tidf_method.py`):
```
1. Home-Office Setup                   score=0.271   ← wrong top pick
2. Work From Home Reimbursement        score=0.158
```

**BM25 result** (`search/keyword_search/bm25_method.py`):
```
1. Work From Home Reimbursement        score=1.333   ← correct
2. Home-Office Setup                   score=0.614
```

Even between two keyword methods, results already disagree. Once Lab 2
(semantic search) is added, the expectation is it should rank
"Work From Home Reimbursement" clearly first *regardless* of exact wording,
since it understands "money back" ≈ "reimbursement" and "working from home"
≈ "remote".

