## Code example: keyword search (already in this project)

`search/keyword_search/bm25_method.py`:
```python
from rank_bm25 import BM25Okapi

class BM25Search:
    def __init__(self, docs):
        self.tokenized_docs = [doc.lower().split() for doc in docs]
        self.bm25 = BM25Okapi(self.tokenized_docs)

    def get_scores(self, query):
        tokenized_query = query.lower().split()
        return self.bm25.get_scores(tokenized_query)
```

## Code example: semantic search (Lab 2, not built yet — preview)

Same `get_scores(query)` interface as `BM25Search`/`TfidfSearch`, so it
will plug straight into the existing `run_test_queries()` in
`search/keyword_search/utils.py` with no changes needed elsewhere:

```python
from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer, util

class SemanticSearch:
    def __init__(self, docs):
        self.model = SentenceTransformer("all-MiniLM-L6-v2")
        self.doc_embeddings = self.model.encode(docs, convert_to_tensor=True)

    def get_scores(self, query):
        query_embedding = self.model.encode(query, convert_to_tensor=True)
        scores = util.cos_sim(query_embedding, self.doc_embeddings)
        return scores[0].cpu().numpy()
```

